anged.\n\n**The rule.** Find the largest-area axis-aligned rectangle filled entirely with one non-background colour. Keep it and set every other cell to background. Noise objects are at most 2 cells, so this choice is clear-cut in every case.\n\n**Test input.** The colour-5 object covers rows 10–11 × cols 5–10, which is a 2×6 = 12-cell rectangle. It also has an extra 5 at (12,5). The output should keep only the 2×6 rectangle.\n\n**How the program builds it.**\n1. Search every rectangle; on a 16×16 grid brute force is fast. Use prefix sums per colour to check whether a box is uniform.\n2. Emit stage: allocate a blank background canvas.\n3. Emit stage: stamp the winning rectangle onto that canvas.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    best = None  # (area, colour, y0, x0, y1, x1)\n    for c in np.unique(g):\n        if c == bg:\n            continue\n        m = (g == c).astype(int)\n        P = np.zeros((H + 1, W + 1), int)\n        P[1:, 1:] = m.cumsum(0).cumsum(1)\n        for y0 in range(H):\n            for y1 in range(y0, H):\n                for x0 in range(W):\n                    for x1 in range(x0, W):\n                        area = (y1 - y0 + 1) * (x1 - x0 + 1)\n                        if best is not None and area <= best[0]:\n                            continue\n                        s = P[y1+1, x1+1] - P[y0, x1+1] - P[y1+1, x0] + P[y0, x0]\n                        if s == area:\n                            best = (area, int(c), y0, x0, y1, x1)\n                        else:\n                            break  # wider boxes in this row range also fail\n    out = np.full_like(g, bg)\n    emit(out, \"Allocate a blank background canvas; all scattered noise will be discarded.\")\n    if best is not None:\n        area, c, y0, x0, y1, x1 = best\n        out[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] = c\n        emit(out, f\"Stamp the largest solid single-colour rectangle (colour {c}, rows {y0}-{y1}, cols {x0}-{x1}); stray attached cells are dropped.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The details show that the rule keeps the largest solid rectangle, not the whole object:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**The rule.** Find the largest-area axis-aligned rectangle filled entirely with one non-background colour."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the largest solid single-colour rectangle (colour 6, rows 11-12, cols 2-8); stray attached cells are dropped."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**The rule.** Find the largest-area axis-aligned rectangle filled entirely with one non-background colour."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Emit stage: stamp the winning rectangle onto that canvas."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the largest solid single-colour rectangle (colour 6, rows 11-12, cols 2-8); stray attached cells are dropped."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the largest solid single-colour rectangle (colour 2, rows 3-6, cols 3-5); stray attached cells are dropped."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Emit stage: allocate a blank background canvas."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a blank background canvas; all scattered noise will be discarded."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"33bea8dc4d62aa3f838d17caafa0b82592591942a3e48ea8e5125b0ee593a739","task_sha256":"93e52ee5f7656f92e80bbe5f50376990250c6dd038f80bf6e3e23fb1985d12af","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
